B.a96=new A.nm("What is a Semaphore?","A semaphore is a synchronization primitive used to control access to shared resources. It's an integer variable that can only be accessed through two atomic operations:\n\n\u2022 **wait (P)**: Decrements the semaphore value\n\u2022 **signal (V)**: Increments the semaphore value\n\nUsed to prevent race conditions in concurrent programming.")
B.a94=new A.nm("Explain Deadlock and its four conditions","Deadlock occurs when two or more processes are waiting for each other indefinitely.\n\n**Four Necessary Conditions (Coffman's):**\n1. **Mutual Exclusion** \u2014 Resource held exclusively\n2. **Hold & Wait** \u2014 Process holds one resource, waits for others\n3. **No Preemption** \u2014 Resources cannot be forcefully taken\n4. **Circular Wait** \u2014 Circular chain of waiting processes")
B.a97=new A.nm("What is Thrashing?","Thrashing occurs when a process spends more time in paging (swapping pages) than executing actual instructions.\n\n**Cause:** Too many processes compete for limited memory frames, causing continuous page faults.\n\n**Solution:** Working Set Model \u2014 allocate frames based on the process's actual working set size.")
B.a95=new A.nm("Difference between Process and Thread?","**Process:**\n\u2022 Independent execution unit\n\u2022 Separate memory space\n\u2022 Heavyweight \u2014 context switch is expensive\n\u2022 Communication via IPC\n\n**Thread:**\n\u2022 Lightweight subprocess within a process\n\u2022 Shares memory with parent process\n\u2022 Faster context switch\n\u2022 Communication via shared memory")
